A||N||5||MikeSchaefer||Raising (or lowering) Question...||||5||
Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||09-29-2000||01:45 AM||||Hi,<BR>I bought my 84 and it was lowered 2" all the way around using the Fiero Store's sport springs. I kind of want the car to have a stance, and have been thinking of rasing the rear end back up to stock, while leaving the front lowered. What affects could this have on handling/steering if any?<BR>Thanks in advance,<BR>Michael Schaefer  <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A>  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||09-29-2000||02:24 AM||||if you lift the rear up 2" it will dump alot more weight on the front. that would make the rear alot lighter and would make alot more oversteer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||09-29-2000||04:39 AM||||I think Batboy had that lower front end look<BR>but the batmobil has the V8 thing? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but it did look nice that way.<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000003||MikeSchaefer||09-29-2000||05:16 AM||||Hi, thanks for the replies.  So would adding a large front swaybar be a neccessity?<BR>Thanks again,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000004||JohnnyK||09-29-2000||04:41 PM||||Well, seeing that the Fiero has way to much weight in the back anyways, all I could think of is that it would help?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||09-29-2000||05:00 PM||||MikeSchaefer:<BR>     Xtreme Fieros is almost right. You might notice that effect if you raised the rear a foot, but 2" will not significantly impact weight distribution or transfer.<BR>     In my opinion, there will be subtle, but small effects on handling from raising the rear.<BR>     Your car already has a front sway bar (7/8"). Adding a 5/8 rear bar should have positive effects on handling.<P>     I must go on record as saying that in general I do not encourage lowering a car. I also whole heartedly disagree with making a performance modification for aesthetic purposes.||||reg||1
